dbe-7450-8db0-ea0044288712", "psp_version_v2": "01a10b87-c8d3-7003-9643-43fa0dcb4742", "psp_version_v3": "01a10b87-d120-7ee1-9615-a52ac69d20ee"}, "model_usage": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": {"inputTokens": 4068, "outputTokens": 6573, "thinkingTokens": 596, "cacheReadInputTokens": 346880, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 35451, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.28398550000000006, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "canonicalModel": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "claude_code_version": "2.1.289", "debrief": "Nothing blocked me, but a few things were awkward.\n\n1. **Invalidation warnings don't say why they fired.** The PostToolUse hook warned that my edits might invalidate \"Invoice PDF rendering\" (01a10b84-b606), but I had only edited type hints in two files that have nothing to do with PDFs. The warning didn't show which `invalidated_by` or `physical` glob matched, so I had to reason it out myself. I wanted the matched path or glob in the hook text. I also wanted a way to dismiss a false positive without calling `challenge`, which would wrongly flag a memory that is still correct. A `dismiss` or `acknowledge` action on the warning, or a `reason` parameter on `verify`, would have covered that.\n\n2. **The same warning kept firing on an intentional edit.** I had already updated memory 01a10b86-8885 to 14 days, but it warned again on each edit to `renewals.py`, and I only cleared it by calling `verify` at the end. I wanted the hook to suppress or downgrade the warning once the memory was updated or verified in the same session.\n\n3. **`verify` records nothing about what was checked.** It stamps `verified_at`, but I had no parameter to say what I checked it against. For example, I would have noted that `RENEWAL_NOTICE_DAYS = 14` and `reminder_due` use the same value. An `evidence` or `source_file` parameter on `verify` would give the stamp a trail.\n\n4. **No link between related memories.** \"Renewal reminder timing\" and \"When renewals run\" (06:00 local time) both feed `reminder_due`. `supersedes` is the only relation field. I wanted a `related` or `links` parameter on `create` and `update` so a query on one surfaces the other.\n\n5. **`verify` was deferred, so I had to load it with ToolSearch first.** That cost a step, though it was only a small one.\n\nI did not save anything for the stateless-reminder gap (no \"reminder sent\" field). That was my choice, not a tool limitation.", "debrief_cost_usd": 0.37073770000000006, "retries": 0}, "rep": 0}
